concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-59a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "59A Unauthorised use of information included in a healthcare"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-59a ;
    values:originalText "recipient’s My Health Record for prohibited purpose  (1) A person must not use health information included in a healthcare recipient’s My Health Record for a prohibited purpose, if the person obtained the information by using or gaining access to the My Health Record system. Note: For prohibited purpose, see section 70A. Civil penalty: 1,500 penalty units.  Schedule 1  Amendments  My Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018 No. 154, 2018  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person is the healthcare recipient, but does apply if the person is the nominated representative of the healthcare recipient (despite subsection 7(2))." ;
    skos:definition "recipient’s My Health Record for prohibited purpose  (1) A person must not use health information included in a healthcare recipient’s My Health Record for a prohibited purpose, if the person obtained the information by using or gaining access to the My Health Record system. Note: For prohibited purpose, see section 70A. Civil penalty: 1,500 penalty units.  Schedule 1  Amendments  My Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018 No. 154, 2018  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person is the healthcare recipient, but does apply if the person is the nominated representative of the healthcare recipient (despite subsection 7(2))."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fc096c3d303d7a9e473439189854c4fa76daab5a7ae5490760a1d940b9323b36" ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-59a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-59a-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
