concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-87 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "87 Acting appointments"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-87 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as the Chair:  (a) during a vacancy in the office of Chair (whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office); or  (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Chair:  (i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or  (ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as the Deputy Chair:  (a) during a vacancy in the office of Deputy Chair (whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office); or  Schedule 2  Amendments commencing on Proclamation  My Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018 No. 154, 2018  (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Deputy Chair:  (i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or  (ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as the Chair:  (a) during a vacancy in the office of Chair (whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office); or  (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Chair:  (i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or  (ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as the Deputy Chair:  (a) during a vacancy in the office of Deputy Chair (whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office); or  Schedule 2  Amendments commencing on Proclamation  My Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018 No. 154, 2018  (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Deputy Chair:  (i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or  (ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bd79508ec41191e591670e8a16396edb8b4de9002381fcff622852525fed9771" ;
    cof:pageNumber "25"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-87-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-87-ss-2 ;
